<title>FRANCE: Cofinoga, Credit Communal in store card venture.</title>
<headline>Cofinoga, Credit Communal in store card venture.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cofinoga, a unit of the French department store group Galeries Lafayette, said it would set up with Credit Communal de Belgique a new firm to develop department store credit cards to be marketed to individuals in Belgium.</p>
<p>Cofinoga said it would hold 49 percent of the capital of the new firm while 51 percent would be held by Comptoir d'Escompte de Belgique, a wholly owned subsidiary of Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB).</p>
<p>CCB is part of the Franco-Belgian banking group Dexia formed by last year's merger of CCB and Credit Local de France.</p>
